\fs48 \cf2 Stepping not supported on GPU\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The step commands\'97Step Over, Step Into, and Step Out do not work reliably on GPU. Instead we recommend adding breakpoints and using Continue to move between breakpoints.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Changing kernel focus\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 You can use CUDA-GDB commands to change the current kernel focus: that is, the block and thread index that you're currently inspecting. Use the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 cuda
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to inspect the current focus or change focus:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf15 \cb14 cuda block thread\cb1 \
\cb14 block (0,0,0), thread (0,0,0)\cb1 \
\cb14 cuda block 0,0,0 thread 1,0,0\cb1 \
\cb14 [Switching focus to CUDA kernel 0, grid 1, block (0,0,0), thread (1,0,0), device 0, sm 0, warp 0, lane 1]\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf18 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf19 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
